{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory","id":837116,"title":"Demon/Promethean crossover theory","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-25T11:35:07-08:00","id":837116,"title":"Demon/Promethean crossover theory","content":"So, I've been working on this for a while, and I should probably come back to it after 2e comes out, but here's a little God-Machine-inclusive theory about where the Divine Fire comes from. <br /> <br /> So, as it turns out, the &quot;god&quot; that the Divine Fire was stolen from was actually the God-Machine, and it wasn't so much stolen as &quot;illegally downloaded and tampered with&quot;. See, a Demon or group of Demons waaaaaay back in the ancient reaches of antiquity managed to corrupt some of the God-Machine's Aether. <br /> <br /> They essentially turned it into a self-replicating angel virus that acts by increasing anthropomorphic tendencies, with the goal of pushing infected angels towards falling. The God-Machine was essentially forced to do a full product recall, modifying its angels to &quot;vaccinate&quot; them and wipe out the &quot;stolen fire&quot; virus. <br /> <br /> But this piece of corrupted divine machinery had begun to act like an actual virus- it mutated and jumped hosts in an effort to preserve itself. The mutated strain couldn't effect &quot;vaccinated&quot; angels, but it could potentially effect anything unliving that had the barest anthropic potential- at first, it could only infect objects with existing human architecture- meaning that it could effectively reanimate the dead. Another mutant strain, however, soon emerged that could effect entirely nonliving matter, provided that some sort of &quot;spark&quot; designated it as having the potential to be &quot;awakened&quot; (by spark, I mean a sort of designator- like a statue being built in a human shape and having humanity &quot;imprinted&quot; on it by a shaman, or an artificial intelligence designed to mimic humanity). <br /> <br /> The God Machine originally waged an aggressive campaign to wipe out this &quot;divine fire&quot;, but found it impossible- or calculated that it was an unwise allocation of resources. The virus was too flighty to be pinned down, and it was devilishly hard to detect. Not only that, but the crusade gave Demon Rings plenty of chances to trick and trap the machine's agents, as well as assaulting Infrastructure left unguarded. The Machine also realized that some of the infected eventually became completely human, effectively neutralizing their threat potential. Eventually, the Machine ended its attempt to wipe out the Divine Fire- though some believe it did leave one protective mechanism: Disquiet. A passive, omnipresent defense against the spread of the virus, and one that would limit the potential of the infected as well as providing incentive for them to become human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T11:51:24-08:00","id":837130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory#post837116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been working on this for a while, and I should probably come back to it after 2e comes out, but here's a little God-Machine-inclusive theory about where the Divine Fire comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh nice! Theorycrafting and universe-building discussion about the relationship between the GM and the Principle!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, as it turns out, the &quot;god&quot; that the Divine Fire was stolen from was actually the God-Machine[...] </div> </div> </div>...aaaaaand you've lost my interest in a single sentence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They essentially turned it into a self-replicating angel virus that acts by increasing anthropomorphic tendencies, with the goal of pushing infected angels towards falling. The God-Machine was essentially forced to do a full product recall, modifying its angels to &quot;vaccinate&quot; them and wipe out the &quot;stolen fire&quot; virus.<br /> <br /> But this piece of corrupted divine machinery had begun to act like an actual virus- it mutated and jumped hosts in an effort to preserve itself. The mutated strain couldn't effect &quot;vaccinated&quot; angels, but it could potentially effect anything unliving that had the barest anthropic potential- at first, it could only infect objects with existing human architecture- meaning that it could effectively reanimate the dead. Another mutant strain, however, soon emerged that could effect entirely nonliving matter, provided that some sort of &quot;spark&quot; designated it as having the potential to be &quot;awakened&quot; (by spark, I mean a sort of designator- like a statue being built in a human shape and having humanity &quot;imprinted&quot; on it by a shaman, or an artificial intelligence designed to mimic humanity).<br /> <br /> The God Machine originally waged an aggressive campaign to wipe out this &quot;divine fire&quot;, but found it impossible- or calculated that it was an unwise allocation of resources. The virus was too flighty to be pinned down, and it was devilishly hard to detect. Not only that, but the crusade gave Demon Rings plenty of chances to trick and trap the machine's agents, as well as assaulting Infrastructure left unguarded. The Machine also realized that some of the infected eventually became completely human, effectively neutralizing their threat potential. Eventually, the Machine ended its attempt to wipe out the Divine Fire- though some believe it did leave one protective mechanism: Disquiet. A passive, omnipresent defense against the spread of the virus, and one that would limit the potential of the infected as well as providing incentive for them to become human. </div> </div> </div>Now in all honesty, this is a really interesting take on Prometheans <i>in a Demon game</i>. I'm somehow lost as to why this theory was posted on the Promethean board rather than the Demon one. My reasons for not liking it in a Promethean game:<br /> <br /> 1- It continues the infamous &quot;GM metaplot&quot;, whereas everything is linked to the GM, created by it, or at war with it. In a Demon game, it's fine. Not so much in a Promethean one.<br /> 2- It reduces the Prometheans to the very concept of Virus. It defines them as parasites working to destroy the God Machine. While this can be an interesting take in a Demon game, it would make me roll my eyes out of my skull as a Promethean player.<br /> 3- It says Prometheans are created to infect Angels, and yet they simply can't do such a thing<br /> 4- It turns the Principle into... a mission to destroy the GM? Their shared code? A side GM? I didn't quite understand that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T13:54:58-08:00","id":837203,"title":"","content":"Agreed with Magnum Opus. Mind you, <b>Promethean</b> has a history with the God-Machine, being the first gameline to publish a chapter featuring an encounter with the GM; so I don't have a problem with some sort of link being established between the God-Machine and the Principle. But not a causal relationship, with the GM being the source of the Divine Fire. <br /> <br /> The theory I'm more inclined to go with is a variant of the \u201cDivine Demiurge\u201d option that was presented in <b>Magnum Opus</b>*: there was a war in Heaven, and the loser was cast down to Earth where it became the god of this world. That's what the GM is: more \u201cdevil\u201d or \u201cGnostic Demiurge\u201d than \u201cGod\u201d. <br /> <br /> The Principle, meanwhile, is the Creator and the Destroyer in one. It is not of this Earth the way the God-Machine is, but intrudes into this world for Its own inscrutable reasons. If you buy the notion of the Empyrean briefly mentioned in <b>Inferno</b> and <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>, <i>that</i> is the likely abode of the Principle. If you want to juxtapose <b>Promethean</b> against the God-Machine, I'd look more toward the New Dawn: every time a Promethean Redeems, a human enters the world who is not entangled in the GM's machinations, and who has the potential to serve as a monkey wrench in the Machine's gears just by being there. <br /> <br /> Of course, I also tend to think that the Redeemed ought to be presented as being among the best humanity has to offer, sort of like how a naturalized citizen tends to be far more informed and patriotic than a natural-born citizen because the former had to struggle to achieve what the latter inherited. In a similar way, a Redeemed human has the benefit of all the experience she gained during her Pilgrimage, and a much deeper appreciation of the human condition \u2014 which, getting back to the main topic at hand, makes her a natural fit as an advocate for human agency. I'm hoping that <b>Promethean 2e</b> does a better job in this regard than 1e did. But that's a topic for another thread. <br /> <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:10px\">* The book, not the poster; that would just be wrong\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:20:33-08:00","id":838295,"title":"","content":"Didn't Matt state at one point that the GM based its angels on the Quashmalim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T17:45:05-08:00","id":838309,"title":"","content":"I'm much more inclined to describe the God-Machine as the flawed mirror of the Principle than to have the latter originate from the former. Both have angels, but the God-Machine can only create shallow Covers while the Principle can (through a very roundabout process, the Great Work) bring new souls into being. <br /> <br /> Or, to draw upon the much-loathed Mage wording of things, the God-Machine is the Fallen companion to a Supernal Divine Fire.<br /> <br /> Can anyone dredge up wherever the God-Machine was described by an Angel as &quot;The Purpose?&quot; That's my favorite point of comparison to The Principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T18:53:47-08:00","id":838348,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm not really fond of the idea that the GM is just the fake robot god and there's actually a nice shiny benevolent more powerful Actual God. I prefer the idea that the GM is essentially the &quot;ultimate&quot; in terms of power level, because it isn't so much a coherent entity as the sum total of the machinery that runs the universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:01:50-08:00","id":838356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=838348#post838348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm not really fond of the idea that the GM is just the fake robot god and there's actually a nice shiny benevolent more powerful Actual God.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that Demon calls itself tech-/Gnostic/ for a reason, right? The idea of a cruel demiurge ruling over flawed reality while a more benevolent God rules in the world beyond is core to Gnosticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:25:31-08:00","id":838368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=838348#post838348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm not really fond of the idea that the GM is just the fake robot god and there's actually a nice shiny benevolent more powerful Actual God. I prefer the idea that the GM is essentially the &quot;ultimate&quot; in terms of power level, because it isn't so much a coherent entity as the sum total of the machinery that runs the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other way around is not much better in my opinion. But that's not the point. Someone suggested at some point that the God-Machine's status quo is fighting against the Principle's eternal entropy. In such a breakdown I'd much rather see both as overtly powerful beings, fighting for reasons we can't fathom, rather than clearly stating one is stronger than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:43:31-08:00","id":838386,"title":"","content":"The Principle isn't benevolent in a traditional sense. It seems fond of humanity, and considers the development of human souls via the Pilgrimage to be worth its utter devotion, but that doesn't make it benevolent. We can't know what the Principle thinks, qashmallim are completely useless in trying to understand it in any way. The Principle transforms, breaks down, brings things together, all those things. I'm personally quite fond of the idea of the GM trying to uphold the status quo in the face of the Principle's constant change. The Principle doesn't even have any measurable goals like the GM does. As much as the GM is a vast eldritch thing, the Principle is totally ineffable. Both are basically untouchable to Mortal and supernatural interference barring extenuating circumstances.<br /> <br /> But, for the sake of discussion, let's say the Principle actually is benevolent- that it cares about humans. In a Biblical sense, it loves humanity. Not individuals, but humanity- perhaps it can barely even comprehend individuality. If each qashmal is a 'thought' of the Principle, perhaps it sees each human as a thought of humanity as a collective entity, the thing it is in love with. Pyros is sentient, it remembers, and the Pilgrimage is teaching it what humans are like, showing it how to enter a relationship with humanity.<br /> <br /> Only problem is, it can't touch the world without burning it, but that's alright. Humans are changing. Every Promethean teaches it something about how to interact with humanity as Pyros is used and Vitriol accrued. Every New Dawn starts to prepare humanity for the touch of the Divine Fire. Maybe, one day, the Principle will be able to show how much it loves us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T19:47:35-08:00","id":838388,"title":"","content":"The Principle is benevolent in that technically new souls are a good thing for humanity and the world. That doesn't stop it from making the Created suffer horribly or sending Qashmallim that cause plagues and burn towns to the ground; it's utterly lacking in any moral guidelines beyond &quot;make new souls, no matter the cost.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:48:13-08:00","id":838428,"title":"","content":"I don't like one reflecting the other in either direction, really.<br /> <br /> In my game, they are either two fragments of a true Empyreal God that existed long before Irem, Father Wolf, or even the Silver Ladder, that was shattered or killed somehow, or even just chose to extricate itself from our reality. The Principle and the God-Machine in this scheme are more echoes or fragments of the True Purpose than anything else, the Principle having a spark of Its divine creativity and emotion, but lacking purpose, thought or any discernible &quot;mind&quot; as we unserstanding, and the God-Machine carrying Its immense intellect and understanding of the physical laws of reality, but lacking emotion, empathy, flexibility, and morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T20:59:58-08:00","id":838432,"title":"","content":"In my games, they are just two different 'gods' that don't have anything cosmologically to do with each others existence.<br /> <br /> I have tons of fun with them when they conflict with each other, though. Or worse, when they have the same aim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:06:41-08:00","id":838489,"title":"","content":"At the risk of stirring up old cosmologies, I had seen them as aspects of the Weaver and of the Wyrm. The Principle is basically the uncorrupted, form of the Wyrm. The God-Machine is the Weaver, though its sanity could well be in doubt. Not sure where the Wyld fits in here. It certainly isn't either the Principle or the G-M, though. Perhaps the Wyld is damaged somehow, and that is why the Gentry are incapable of being creative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:12:30-08:00","id":838491,"title":"","content":"If anything, the Principle is the Wyld here. While it has has the Lillithim, so far, the only discernable goal we can see from this thing is &quot;create new souls&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:14:04-08:00","id":838492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=838489#post838489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the risk of stirring up old cosmologies, I had seen them as aspects of the Weaver and of the Wyrm. The Principle is basically the uncorrupted, form of the Wyrm. The God-Machine is the Weaver, though its sanity could well be in doubt. Not sure where the Wyld fits in here. It certainly isn't either the Principle or the G-M, though. Perhaps the Wyld is damaged somehow, and that is why the Gentry are incapable of being creative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how you're getting the Wyrm from the only known source of new souls in the CofD cosmology. The closest we have to a Wyrm analogue is either Ammut from Mummy or the entire Abyss in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:19:11-08:00","id":838494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=838492#post838492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure how you're getting the Wyrm from the only known source of new souls in the CofD cosmology. The closest we have to a Wyrm analogue is either Ammut from Mummy or the entire Abyss in Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Although, that would be an interesting twist on the cosmology. I might toy with that for a Mage campaign. I'd probably make the Abyss an alien force, though, and have the Wyrm imprisoned beneath the Underworld (hence the place being so jam-packed with ghosts, that a free Wyrm would normally be nomming upon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:25:50-08:00","id":838498,"title":"","content":"I suppose the Principle could be some shackled form of the Wyld. But given the intensely toxic and mutagenic properties of Azoth, I was uncomfortable with the Wyld identification. ... actually, maybe it's got more in common with the Questing essence which gives the Cosmic Principles their direction. Maybe Azoth is a very dangerous mixture of Wyld and Wyrm energies, and the Principle is the Questing essence which guides them towards a new dawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:27:39-08:00","id":838499,"title":"","content":"If I were to try to port WtA's Triat into the ChroD, my inclination would be to have the Principle represent both the Wyld (in its Elpis/Elpidos/Elpidim/etc. role) and the Wyrm (in its Flux/Torment/Lilithim/etc. role), while the God-Machine would represent the Weaver. I'd probably split the <i>qashmallim</i> into two fundamentally distinct kinds of beings, as opposed to being opposite poles of a magnet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2016, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T23:39:35-08:00","id":838506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vithrir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=838498#post838498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the Principle could be some shackled form of the Wyld. But given the intensely toxic and mutagenic properties of Azoth, I was uncomfortable with the Wyld identification. ... actually, maybe it's got more in common with the Questing essence which gives the Cosmic Principles their direction. Maybe Azoth is a very dangerous mixture of Wyld and Wyrm energies, and the Principle is the Questing essence which guides them towards a new dawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, the Principle exists in Flux every bit as much as it exists in Elpis. It essentially has a split personaliy, where it's building things up one day and tearing them down the next. <br /> <br /> Also: on the Weaver thing, remember that in the WoD, the Weaver is quite mad; I think it's a <i>very</i> good GM analog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T15:59:15-08:00","id":842208,"title":"","content":"I think maybe instead of a Triat, how about a Quadrat? Weaver, Wyld, Wyrm, and Wyrd:<br /> <br /> \u200bWeaver seeks to bring order and stagnation. = GM<br /> Wyld seeks to promote change and creativity. = Principle<br /> Wyrm seeks entropy. = Abyss?<br /> Wyld just wants good stories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T17:50:25-08:00","id":842291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=842208#post842208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think maybe instead of a Triat, how about a Quadrat? Weaver, Wyld, Wyrm, and Wyrd:<br /> <br /> \u200bWeaver seeks to bring order and stagnation. = GM<br /> Wyld seeks to promote change and creativity. = Principle<br /> Wyrm seeks entropy. = Abyss?<br /> Wyld just wants good stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld creates raw materials, the Weaver shapes these materials into props and actors, the Wyrd shapes those into stories and narratives, and the Wyrm then destroys elements that have served their purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T19:42:27-08:00","id":842353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/837116-demon-promethean-crossover-theory?p=842291#post842291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld creates raw materials, the Weaver shapes these materials into props and actors, the Wyrd shapes those into stories and narratives, and the Wyrm then destroys elements that have served their purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've gotten way off topic but honestly this discussion about cosmic forces is more interesting than my original idea so I'm enjoying reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}